          "visualization": {
            "id": "viz.markdown"
          },
          "rawConfiguration": {
            "text": "# README\n\n## About this page\nThis page displays the **advanced-tier** `forwarder.*` custom metrics emitted by the [OCI Log Forwarder](https://github.com/newrelic/oci-log-integration) Function. These metrics are **in addition** to the basic-tier metrics shown on the previous page. They are available when `metrics_tier = advanced` in the Terraform configuration.\n\n## Metrics on this page\n\n### Byte volumes\n- **forwarder.bytes.received** \u2014 raw payload bytes read from the OCI invocation input.\n- **forwarder.bytes.delivered** \u2014 bytes sent to the New Relic Logs API per successful batch.\n\n### Errors\n- **forwarder.decode.errors** \u2014 failures to JSON-decode the incoming OCI event payload (tagged with `error_class`).\n- **forwarder.serialize.errors** \u2014 failures to JSON-marshal individual log entries during batch assembly.\n- **forwarder.records.oversized** \u2014 records that individually exceed the New Relic 1 MB payload limit.\n- **forwarder.delivery.errors** \u2014 delivery errors tagged with `error_class` and `status=error`.\n- **forwarder.secret.fetch.errors** \u2014 failures to fetch the New Relic license key from OCI Vault.\n\n### Batching & performance\n- **forwarder.batches.created** \u2014 number of batches assembled per invocation.\n- **forwarder.batch.size_bytes** \u2014 distribution of batch sizes in bytes (min/avg/max per invocation).\n- **forwarder.run.duration** \u2014 total function run time in seconds (excluding the metrics flush itself).\n\n### Client cache\n- **forwarder.client.cache** \u2014 New Relic client cache outcome tagged with `result=hit` or `result=miss`."
          }
        },
